# Project Context

- This is a Windows-first Among Us community mod launcher built with Go,
  Wails v3, React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and Framer Motion.
- Town of Us: Mira is the first supported mod; platform-specific assets come
  from its GitHub Releases.
- `internal/appservice/` is the Wails API boundary.
- `internal/game/` owns storefront detection and compatibility.
- `internal/installer/` owns download, extraction, and atomic installation.
- `internal/installrecord/` owns launcher-management markers.
- `internal/mods/` contains the registry and shared models.
- `frontend/src/` contains UI source; `frontend/bindings/` is generated.
- Keep backend packages independent of React and keep UI logic out of Go
  packages except through the app service boundary.
- Match CI: Go 1.25+, Node 22+, Wails `v3.0.0-alpha2.117`.
- Git tags (`vX.Y.Z`) are the release-version source of truth.
- Windows releases are currently unsigned, so preserve SmartScreen and SHA256
  guidance until Authenticode signing is implemented.
